WEBVTT

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:15.240
The times evolve at an accelerated rate.

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:20.870
Commonplace values
become things of the past in no time.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:33.050
The window connecting you to the world
gets stronger every day,

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:38.050
and becomes elaborately intertwined
so that no one can control it anymore.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:45.640
Your characteristic is to do things people can't do
in accordance with the input data.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:51.110
Oh, what a waste.

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:53.400
Ouch!

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.370
<i>The Far Eastern Special Administrative Region,</i>

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:32.880
<i>also known as the 24th Ward,
is a man-made island sitting in Tokyo Bay.</i>

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:38.670
<i>Allies ruled over this island after the war,
but due to its special circumstances,</i>

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:42.760
<i>it became famous for being one of
the most dangerous red-light districts in Asia.</i>

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.850
<i>Roughly 20 years has passed</i>

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:48.020
<i>since it's been handed back to Japan
with hopes of restoring peace to the island.</i>

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:53.770
<i>After a long transition period, it was about to be
officially incorporated as a part of Tokyo.</i>

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:59.860
<i>However, because of a certain incident,
a great turn of events takes place.</i>

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:00.700
MAY 10, 2020

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:05.830
You're saying that Asumi
went inside to save Kozue?

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.830
I told her we should wait for you, Shu.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.970
Koki! Aren't the firefighters here yet?

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:12.160
I'm checking right now!

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:16.380
Ko, it's useless. They're in a gridlock from the festival,
so it'll take a bit more time.

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:20.090
Sakuragi, how many minutes has it been
since Asumi went in?

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:21.630
About three minutes.

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:23.340
I can save her.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:25.930
Don't fret so much, Shu.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.560
We need to figure out the actual location first.

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:31.480
Recklessly searching
will only cause you to miss each other.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:34.230
Isn't the coast guard here yet?

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.730
- Water sprays should reach here from fireboats.
- Shu?

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.820
I did say wait.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.070
That idiot.

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:48.870
Wait, Shuta. The building is starting to collapse.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:50.450
I don't care!

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:52.160
Just hold on for a bit.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:54.920
I'm doing a scan
with the thermo-sensor right now.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:00.130
What the hell?

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:03.180
Sorry, I just can't stand still.

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:07.510
Shu!

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:09.520
You too, Mari?

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:13.810
I won't stop you,
so make sure to save both of them!

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:17.230
Of course. I'm a hero after all!

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:34.460
Kozue, where are you?

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.130
Answer me! Mr.24 is here to save you!

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:40.210
Asumi! Kozue!

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:42.670
Asumi. Kozue.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:44.930
Damn it.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:48.390
- Both of you, if you can hear me, answer me!
- Shu.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:51.810
- Shu.
- Kozue? Are you over there?

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:08.700
Kozue.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:11.040
Are you all right? Just hang on.

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:14.710
- I'll move this rubble aside real qui—
- Shu...

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:20.250
Asumi shielded me and...

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:21.170
Asumi.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:25.630
Asumi! Asumi!

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:28.340
Asumi.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.760
- Why... Why?
- Shu...

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:32.180
<i>I couldn't save her.</i>

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:36.850
<i>I...</i>

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.610
<i>...couldn't become a hero.</i>

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:46.030
MAY 8, 2021

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:47.320
What a nightmare.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:49.200
KABA

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:58.080
<i>You awake?</i>

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:01.380
Yeah, totally. See you.

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:09.130
<i>You fell asleep again.</i>

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:10.640
No I didn't.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:14.180
<i>Well, whatever.
You better show up to the memorial mass.</i>

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:15.640
Yeah.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.810
How long will you act like
my homeroom teacher?

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:21.060
How long do you think it's been
since I graduated?

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:26.030
What a bother.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.450
Damn it.

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:33.240
Don't you know how to tie it?

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:35.580
Hey Kiriko, what do you think you're...

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:37.450
Call me "Mom."

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:39.830
How handsome!

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:42.670
Shuta, have you grown some more?

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:44.300
Hey, stop that!

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.800
Maybe you'll grow taller than your father?

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:49.510
No, that's not going to happen.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:52.010
This is bothersome, but I'm heading out.

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:53.390
Oh Shuta.

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:54.390
Take this.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:55.600
Your breakfast!

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.980
Huh? I don't need any.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.850
- But it's fresh out of the oven.
- I said no.

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:01.270
It's our new product.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:12.030
AOI BAKERY

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.990
It's not using Danish dough,
but it's crunchy and fluffy.

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:11.360
The cream inside
isn't a simple demi-glace, either.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:13.910
It's Daisy!

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.910
This has onions in it, so I can't give you any.

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:18.830
Shu!

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:20.250
Grab Daisy for me!

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:23.630
All right! Got you!

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.880
- Mari.
- Whew, that was close.

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:27.760
Thanks, Shu!

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:29.920
It's dangerous to take her out without a leash.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:34.600
That's not it. We were talking about
taking her to the vet when we were in the house.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:36.680
She heard that, got scared, and ran off.

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:38.060
You're taking her to the vet today?

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:43.150
I am. Grandma hurt her back
during the karaoke tournament the other day.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:45.770
- But it's not until the late afternoon.
- Old Ume got hurt again?

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:55.370
OKONOMIYAKI - ITADAKI

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:50.240
I haven't gotten ready yet because I was chasing
Daisy, so can you go ahead without me, Shu?

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.320
- Yeah. Don't be late.
- Yup.

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:55.370
Same for you, Shu.
You better go to the church.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:57.120
I know that.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:01.120
This is the first time since graduation
that you'll be seeing Ran and Koki.

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:07.040
Oh man, I wish I could see
all three of the RGB's in one place.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:10.130
All three of you should drop by our place
after seeing Asumi.

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:11.550
I'll keep a table open for you guys.

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:13.970
I don't even know if they'll show up.

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:16.050
Man, this place is totally deserted.

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:18.180
And a cheap sign, too!

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:22.730
- A strip mall like this should just fold!
- This place looks 30 years old!

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:24.520
That'd be for the better of everyone!

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.440
Mari, take this.

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:29.480
Hey, wait! Sh-Shu?

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:31.780
- The fish I bought at that shop was rotten!
- What're you looking at?

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:33.280
Hey, Pocket.

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:37.870
Huh? Pocket? What're you talking about?

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:39.290
You dropped it.

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:44.670
Huh? What? This look like
a pocket to you, little boy?

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:51.550
You! Are gonna become! A pocket ashtray!

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:57.510
B-Bastard! What're you—

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:02.850
- Good job, Shu!
- Awesome!

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:04.890
- Thank goodness!
- Shuta, please take this!

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:07.100
- Thank you, Shuta!
- Whoa! Thanks, I'll have some!

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:09.730
- How about some apples, too?
- Oh my, they toppled so many.

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:11.480
Shu, you resorted to violence again.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:13.780
Guys like that piss you off, don't they?

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:18.120
I thought you gave up being a hero?

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:22.330
I was never one to begin with.

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:24.910
Ow.

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:27.540
My eyes are flashing.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:29.710
- Get outta here!
- Evil spirits, begone!

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:30.920
- Mom!
- Kiriko.

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:34.550
Damn it, you'll face a lot worse
if you don't hurry up and leave this place.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.180
- Quit your yapping!
- Go home!

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.510
It's for your own good to listen to us!

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:40.010
- Go home!
- Get outta here!

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:44.480
Oh well. I'll be heading out now.

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:46.600
- Okay. I'll see you over there.
- Yeah.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:48.350
Shu, take care.

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:50.310
- Thanks!
- It's nothing.

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:54.240
Shu's the only one who can protect
Takara Shopping Street!

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:56.610
It's getting pretty dangerous lately, too.

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:59.620
He'll get carried away so don't compliment him.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:15.340
Finished!

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:17.930
Here's our new graffiti!

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:24.270
This new piece from DoRed will hack into the 24th Ward
and appear somewhere within the next 24 hours!

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:27.270
Please spread the word
and subscribe to our channel!

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:29.270
DoRed!

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:34.190
Okay, and that's a wrap.
Thanks for everything, Ran!

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:39.610
I'm at my limit. So sleepy.

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:43.780
Kinako, toss this data into the drone.

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:45.660
- Okay.
- I'll do it.

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:46.620
Kunai.

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:48.500
Are you okay?

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:52.170
You have to temporarily shut down the cameras
around the station, don't you?

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:53.670
Preparations are done.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:57.510
Kinako has it harder with the prep
because there're so many little things to do.

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:01.220
Honestly, I would really appreciate your help.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:03.390
- Yeah.
- Kunai, you're so nice.

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:04.720
Lucky, you shut up.

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:06.720
Hey, we're gonna head out soon.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:09.140
- Got it.
- Okey dokey.

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:11.560
Everyone, let's do our best.

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:14.060
- Hey, hurry up.
- Okey dokey.

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:26.200
<i>There are two items on the schedule for today.</i>

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:29.540
<i>Memorial service
for the Takara Elementary fire at 11:00.</i>

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:31.960
<i>Opening ceremony
for the Kizuna Train at 15:00.</i>

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:31.960
Kinako.

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:33.920
Another energy drink.

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:35.170
S-Sure!

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:40.970
Can you get me some clothes?

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:46.350
Ran, overconsumption of energy drinks
is not good for your body.

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:47.970
Money creates money.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:48.890
Huh?

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:55.480
The fastest way to make money
is to use money in a smart way.

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:59.030
So, because little ol' me
wants to create energy,

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:01.700
I borrow some energy in advance
to produce energy.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:02.910
Understand?

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:06.160
Isn't that logic a bit weird?

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:08.790
Well, I'm counting on you
over at the train station.

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:09.450
Okay!

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:22.720
<i>Are you awake?</i>

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:24.220
I haven't slept.

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:26.680
<i>You know, you need to have
a more normal life—</i>

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:28.350
Okay, talk to you later.

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:35.600
Excuse me.

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:41.570
Father, after the memorial services
are over today—

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:45.360
You should be aware that the opening ceremony
for Kizuna is today.

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:48.240
We made sure
the ceremony would happen today.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:51.500
Yes. That's why I don't mind if it's after
the ceremony, but if we could—

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:54.460
I plan on dining
with the governor of Tokyo after that.

00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:59.420
I will be escorting you, Mr. Koki.

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:02.050
Thank you.

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:04.300
- Tsuzuragawa.
- Yes?

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:10.470
There aren't any problems moving up the schedule
for the system upgrade for Hazard Cast, right?

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:11.560
Correct.

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:14.440
Our progress is at 80% already.

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:17.690
I will share the details with you later.

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:19.020
Please do.

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:20.480
Please excuse me.

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:28.280
You're the manager of development, so do you
even have time to keep taking care of me?

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:32.040
I accepted the development lead role
under these conditions.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:35.040
It picks away at my conscience a little bit.

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:37.000
Please don't worry about it.

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:38.000
Oh?

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:42.250
They're hiding amongst the civilians,
but there are several SARG members staking out.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:43.840
Let me check it out.

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:46.840
I see. Something might happen.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:55.140
- This is bad!
- Call the cops!

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:57.480
- Please don't enter here.
- Guide traffic so we can shut down one lane!

00:13:57.480 --> 00:13:59.230
- Stretchers!
- Hurry! We can still make it in time!

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:00.770
Running a red light?

00:14:00.770 --> 00:14:03.030
That is quite a speedy response as expected.

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:06.070
You don't have to go over there, Mr. Koki?

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:10.570
If an intern were to show up on his day off,
it would only trouble everyone over there.

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:11.740
I see.

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:14.580
The victim seems to be conscious, too.

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:16.410
Yeah, that's good news.

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:19.710
Besides, the speed of this response
just demonstrates

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:23.000
what the Special Administrative
Region Guard can do.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:26.090
But in the end, it's only a stopgap measure.

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.760
We can predict crimes,
but we can't make arrests to prevent them.

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:32.560
No one can be charged for a crime
until they commit them.

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:35.930
Yeah, the law hasn't caught up to reality yet.

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:37.230
Not yet for now.

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:39.520
Hello?

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:42.020
<i>Hey, Koki. You're headed over, right?</i>

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:43.730
Yes, I'm currently on the road.

00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:46.280
<i>You know what's going on
after the memorial mass, right?</i>

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:48.200
Yes. I have no issues.

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:50.450
I'm bracing myself for it though.

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:54.870
<i>Take it easy. I'm sure you guys can do it.</i>

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:56.870
I sure hope so.

00:14:56.870 --> 00:14:58.120
<i>I'll talk to you later.</i>

00:14:58.120 --> 00:14:59.080
Okay.

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:03.040
Is everyone headed to Ms. Asumi's place
in the afternoon?

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:03.960
Yeah.

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:05.050
Your ride?

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:07.590
I'm fine, Mr. Shirakaba said he'll drive.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:09.050
The usual trio?

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:11.590
We'll see about that. Will they show up?

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:13.260
I'm worried.

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:15.430
Tsuzuragawa, don't put one on me.

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:16.970
Yes.

00:15:16.970 --> 00:15:19.140
You absolutely should not
be putting one on me.

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:20.020
Yes.

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:22.940
That's not an invitation.

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:23.860
Right.

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:30.150
I will head over after parking the car.

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:33.780
Yeah. Thank you for helping me.
I can get home by myself.

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:38.700
Mr. Koki, Miss Asumi would be pouting
if you dropped by empty-handed.

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:41.460
Indeed. Sorry about that.

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:51.680
A tracker. At least it's not a bug transmitter.

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:57.430
TAKARA ELEMENTARY SCHOOL FIRE
FIRST ANNIVERSARY MEMORIAL MASS

00:15:58.560 --> 00:15:59.680
<i>Of course this is what happens.</i>

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:01.640
Why are you here?

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:03.060
Personal freedom.

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:05.020
More like, why did you think
we wouldn't be here?

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:07.110
Oh, right.

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:11.320
Mari? How did she get here before I did?

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:12.990
She framed me.

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:15.280
I was thinking Kaba was a bit persistent.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:16.950
Sakuragi is in on this, too.

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:19.540
Well, it was a situation
that was waiting to happen.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:22.960
Hey Shu, you're way too careless
with your feet.

00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:27.040
Do you know
what Time, Place, Occasion means?

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:30.050
F-Feelings are what's important
for occasions like this!

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:48.070
May she rest in peace under God's care.
We shall put our hearts together and pray.

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:53.320
With love, we shall pray.
Our hopes and prayers...

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:52.780
Hey, this past year, have you...

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:55.360
No, never mind.

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:57.870
There's nothing to "never mind" about.

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:01.910
We don't gather up
unless we have stuff like this nowadays.

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:08.670
<i>We will now begin the first anniversary memorial mass
for the Takara Elementary School Fire.</i>

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:11.760
It's been a year since that loathsome incident.

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:15.760
We have lost precious lives.

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:19.140
I myself have lost a family member.

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:25.390
We have scientific proof that it was arson,
but we still cannot find the perpetrator.

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:28.610
It's all because there are no eyewitnesses.

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:32.030
Ko, your dad really utilizes
everything he can, doesn't he?

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:34.990
I won't deny that. It makes for good politics.

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:38.160
You don't blindly believe him, do you?

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:42.240
The problem is whether or not he's right.

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:45.620
Anyway, are you going there after this?

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:50.250
Kaba went ahead
and set everything up already, right?

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:52.960
Both Kaba and Mari
meddle into people's business too much.

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:55.010
You're spoiled by Sakuragi too much.

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:56.550
I agree there.

00:17:57.090 --> 00:17:58.390
By the way, Mari...

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:02.720
<i>On that note, we will end
the first anniversary memorial mass</i>

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:06.100
<i>for the Takara Elementary School Fire.</i>

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:11.270
Huh? Kozue?

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:14.940
Kozue, you're almost at the medical office.

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:15.530
Okay.

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:18.910
<i>I'm sorry! I'm sorry!</i>

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:23.200
Sorry for calling you guys out here.

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:26.410
I got an emergency right now,
so kill some time for me.

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:28.620
That's fine, but more importantly...

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:30.290
Is Kozuetchi all right?

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:32.130
You saw all that, huh?

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:36.220
I heard rumors
that she's refusing to go to school.

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:39.550
Yeah. She went through a lot
since that incident.

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:43.600
She stopped going to school,
and she even stopped going outside her home.

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:45.180
Sorry about all this.

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:48.310
You're all victims as well,
but I'm having you guys be considerate.

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:52.440
I half-forced you guys out today
because it was a memorial mass.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:54.150
I guess it was a mistake.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:55.900
Of course it wasn't.

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:58.990
It's a bit complicated with Kozue, right?

00:18:58.990 --> 00:19:01.320
I want to understand
how she feels, even a little bit.

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:05.950
So, with that said, I would like to be
at Kozue's side for a bit.

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:07.960
I'll send you guys a text
when she settles down.

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:10.460
What are you guys gonna do?

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:14.550
If I have some time now, I'd like to take care
of several items on my agenda. See you.

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:16.920
Little ol' me got some things to do, too.

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:22.220
Man, they're so busy.

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:29.890
I haven't been here for a while,
but does it feel a bit different now?

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:32.690
They changed the sign three months ago.

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:34.900
- Chikuwa!
- You're calling a superior by his nickname?

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:36.820
That's so unpleasant.

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:39.780
Listen up. My name is Wataru Chikushi.

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:42.620
I told you that multiple times
when I was setting you back on the right path.

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:45.030
Thanks for taking care of me then.

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:47.790
It was nothing.
And pull your hands out of your pockets.

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:50.460
Anyway, what does a SARG inspector
want with me?

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:53.330
You'd call out to someone
if you recognize them on the street, right?

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:55.840
I guess that makes sense.

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:57.250
Hey, Shuta.

00:19:57.710 --> 00:19:59.510
Do you know about a group called DoRed?

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:01.590
- Nope.
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:03.050
You're so heartless.

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:06.140
Hey, do you still interact with Ran Akagi?

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:07.310
No way.

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:09.890
Hey! Don't run from me!

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:17.730
Next time, I'll head over to Itadaki again!
You have to tell me your story!

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:22.910
Sheesh, what's going on?
Did Ran do something again?

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:25.030
Is everything according to plan?

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:26.830
<i>- Yes. How is it?
- Hi, Ran! How are you?</i>

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:29.500
I have good reception. No complaints here.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:33.710
Looks like we'll get some good footage here.
I'll be counting on you when we go live.

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:34.790
<i>Ran.</i>

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:39.050
<i>I got intel from Kunai
that they increased security personnel.</i>

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:42.010
Oh? I guess SARG ain't all dummies?

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:45.800
<i>We won't get doxxed, right?
Ran, if you get arrested, I...</i>

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:48.930
You know what hacking techniques
little ol' me has, yeah?

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:51.730
<i>I know about that, but the risks...</i>

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:54.690
I don't like it.

00:20:55.060 --> 00:21:01.690
Gori Suido's policies claim that control
will provide a more stable lifestyle.

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:03.570
But in the end, it's nothing but lip service.

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:08.950
They added bias to the Hazard Cast numbers,
and minorities are hunted down without any regard.

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:13.000
<i>Even the other day, the SARG
was scoring brownie points over in Shantytown.</i>

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:16.500
There are more guys that just get desperate
and resort to committing crimes.

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:19.840
And who's the one
disrupting the peace in Shantytown?

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:22.760
We're not gonna go along with that guy's rules.

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:23.840
Right.

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:25.720
<i>Well, I'll contact you later.</i>

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:26.510
Okay.

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:34.940
Oh, whoops.

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:40.230
It should be somewhere around here.

00:21:41.730 --> 00:21:42.940
This is it.

00:21:43.440 --> 00:21:45.280
The other one is over there.

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:49.030
This is basically saying
you'll be committing a crime here.

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:52.660
The number of cameras being vandalized
are increasing lately.

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:55.500
Is it resistance against Hazard Cast?

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:59.460
I guess I'll send a confirmation report
to the Management Division.

00:22:01.630 --> 00:22:02.840
Was I imagining things?

00:22:06.880 --> 00:22:10.510
<i>Mon, Mon, Mon, Mon Jungle!</i>

00:22:10.600 --> 00:22:15.850
<i>- Mon, Mon, Mon, Mon Jungle!
- Oh! Let's go to Mon Jungle!</i>

00:22:15.850 --> 00:22:19.060
The Mon Jungle commercial is so surreal.

00:22:19.310 --> 00:22:21.270
Chikuwa made me all hungry.

00:22:21.270 --> 00:22:23.820
Now, time to fill my stomach before the war.

00:22:23.820 --> 00:22:26.320
Monja, huh? No...

00:22:26.320 --> 00:22:28.320
ITADAKI

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:28.320
It's gotta be okonomiyaki.

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:33.790
OKONOMIYAKI - ITADAKI

00:22:29.280 --> 00:22:30.410
Again?

00:22:30.410 --> 00:22:31.780
In the end...

00:22:31.780 --> 00:22:33.790
You're here, RGB!

00:22:33.790 --> 00:22:37.580
It's a bit earlier than I was planning for,
but oh well. Come on in!

00:22:35.580 --> 00:22:37.580
- Hey, now.
- Maririn!

00:22:42.290 --> 00:22:45.170
Shuta, you're invading my territory.
Keep yours closer to the edge.

00:22:45.760 --> 00:22:48.050
If I get any closer to the edge,
it'll lose its shape!

00:22:48.050 --> 00:22:49.510
Koki, move yours.

00:22:50.890 --> 00:22:52.890
Hey! Both of you, don't argue!

00:22:55.640 --> 00:22:58.770
Just how much are you pouring on?
You're turning into o-mayo-yaki!

00:22:58.770 --> 00:22:59.650
Bonito flakes.

00:22:58.770 --> 00:23:00.810
I don't appreciate you playing with your food.

00:23:00.940 --> 00:23:03.440
Sprinkle some seaweed...

00:23:03.730 --> 00:23:04.900
Finished!

00:23:05.530 --> 00:23:07.570
- What? This thing...
- How dexterous.

00:23:08.150 --> 00:23:09.660
Looks photogenic, right?

00:23:09.740 --> 00:23:11.370
Looks like it could easily go viral, but...

00:23:11.370 --> 00:23:14.410
I'll feel bad eating it, so stop it.

00:23:14.620 --> 00:23:18.250
Anything with shape, in due time, will all...

00:23:18.370 --> 00:23:19.370
break!

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:21.000
Creak, creak!

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:22.500
No hesitation!

00:23:23.170 --> 00:23:27.210
Graffiti is art destined to be erased
from the moment of creation.

00:23:27.720 --> 00:23:31.300
That's why when you gaze upon it now,
it emotionally resonates with you.

00:23:31.300 --> 00:23:32.930
You're like a seaside Picasso.

00:23:32.930 --> 00:23:35.390
- Sea? P-Pica?
- Is that why you started DoRed?

00:23:35.600 --> 00:23:37.680
Hmm, let's see.

00:23:37.680 --> 00:23:40.480
It's already been a while since I started it up.

00:23:40.480 --> 00:23:42.270
I've been wanting to ask you.

00:23:42.270 --> 00:23:44.400
You're gathering more members
from the internet, right?

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:46.230
It was called DoRed, right?

00:23:46.230 --> 00:23:49.240
Chikuwa from SARG
asked me about you earlier.

00:23:49.240 --> 00:23:50.860
Sorry to trouble you.

00:23:51.320 --> 00:23:54.660
It's true that SARG has their eyes on us lately.

00:23:54.910 --> 00:23:58.950
What about you, Ko? You're helping daddy Gori out
while going to college?

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:02.670
I have my own thoughts about this,
and that's why I'm interning at SARG.

00:24:02.670 --> 00:24:05.210
Huh? Seriously? Koki, you're gonna join SARG?

00:24:05.210 --> 00:24:07.590
No way! I want to become a politician.

00:24:07.840 --> 00:24:11.680
The Special Administrative Region Guard
is a police organization funded by Suido Zaibatsu,

00:24:11.680 --> 00:24:14.510
so it's true that it was easy to join them.

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:17.470
But more importantly,
they deal with Hazard Cast.

00:24:17.470 --> 00:24:19.560
A lot of elements are there
that I want to learn about.

00:24:19.560 --> 00:24:21.770
Hacking into real life based on art.

00:24:22.190 --> 00:24:26.270
Real life is operated
based on a certain set of rules and principles.

00:24:26.900 --> 00:24:30.690
And those rules were created by the powerful,
so the weak get tormented.

00:24:30.690 --> 00:24:35.530
So I plan to hack into those rules
and run an update on society as a whole.

00:24:35.530 --> 00:24:37.410
But that art you draw is unauthorized, right?

00:24:37.410 --> 00:24:38.870
It's called "street art."

00:24:39.290 --> 00:24:42.790
Damage to property and buildings,
which is quite the misdemeanor.

00:24:42.790 --> 00:24:44.420
If you go too far, you'll get arrested.

00:24:44.420 --> 00:24:48.090
By you, Ko?
The political crime of illegal art?

00:24:48.420 --> 00:24:52.680
But the 24th Ward is in a transition period
with its incorporation into Tokyo, isn't it?

00:24:52.680 --> 00:24:54.720
Doesn't the SARG
have more important things—

00:24:54.720 --> 00:24:56.930
Discipline is important
especially during a transition period.

00:24:56.930 --> 00:25:00.060
But who is that discipline for?

00:25:00.060 --> 00:25:03.730
You guys really are thinking things out
and then taking action, huh?

00:25:03.730 --> 00:25:07.190
Yeah. You're like adults.
So different from Shu.

00:25:09.690 --> 00:25:16.240
Well, Ko might just be riding the rails daddy Gori
laid out for him as the heir to the Suido Zaibatsu.

00:25:16.240 --> 00:25:19.700
I'm riding the rails because I feel
I have a responsibility for all the passengers.

00:25:19.790 --> 00:25:23.040
I can't let the train called 24th Ward derail.

00:25:24.580 --> 00:25:25.460
So...

00:25:25.580 --> 00:25:26.710
What about you, Shu?

00:25:27.960 --> 00:25:29.170
Shu!

00:25:29.170 --> 00:25:32.920
It's been almost a year since we graduated
from high school. What about you?

00:25:32.920 --> 00:25:34.930
What about me? About what?

00:25:34.930 --> 00:25:36.800
A total NEET now!

00:25:37.010 --> 00:25:38.430
You won't take over the bakery?

00:25:38.760 --> 00:25:41.060
I do help out my family.

00:25:41.060 --> 00:25:44.020
But I started thinking that what if I simply
became an adult like this?

00:25:44.020 --> 00:25:46.690
Then what would Asumi say?

00:25:46.940 --> 00:25:50.400
Don't blame Asumi
for your inability to move forward.

00:25:50.400 --> 00:25:53.490
If you let the dead trap you forever,
she won't be able to rest in peace.

00:25:53.490 --> 00:25:57.820
Shu, are you done with the hero stuff you did
back when you were a student?

00:25:57.820 --> 00:25:59.490
I actually liked that about you.

00:25:59.870 --> 00:26:02.870
Oh, all the hero stuff?
I just don't feel confident about it.

00:26:02.870 --> 00:26:04.750
Hey, what's with the serious answer?

00:26:04.750 --> 00:26:07.370
Oh no, that's so like Shu to do that.

00:26:07.370 --> 00:26:10.210
And that incident happened because of it!
He needs to think about the future more—

00:26:10.210 --> 00:26:11.460
It's done!

00:26:11.750 --> 00:26:14.800
Today's Mari-Special is Blue Hawaii Calamari!

00:26:15.050 --> 00:26:17.970
I wanted to represent squids
swimming in the tropical seas!

00:26:17.970 --> 00:26:20.470
<i>Here it comes.
Looks like it's a "miss" day.</i>

00:26:20.470 --> 00:26:22.640
<i>Maririn, your talent is overflowing.</i>

00:26:22.640 --> 00:26:24.810
<i>Huh? But this is blue...</i>

00:26:24.810 --> 00:26:26.190
<i>I'm sure it tastes awful!</i>

00:26:26.390 --> 00:26:31.570
<i>Mari's Special is the signature dish,
so she'll complain if we don't eat it.</i>

00:26:31.570 --> 00:26:35.360
<i>There's a need to accurately communicate
my impressions that it tastes awful.</i>

00:26:35.360 --> 00:26:40.410
<i>This is art! I can't let the experience
of Mari-Special disappear from the Itadaki menu!</i>

00:26:40.490 --> 00:26:42.790
<i>That means I need to eat all of it.</i>

00:26:45.250 --> 00:26:47.750
Oh! Hey! Don't play with your food!

00:26:51.170 --> 00:26:53.000
A phone call? Man, that scared me.

00:26:53.000 --> 00:26:55.590
- All three of us at once?
- It's too good but it's true.

00:26:55.590 --> 00:26:56.470
ASUMIN

00:26:55.590 --> 00:26:56.470
ASUMI

00:26:55.590 --> 00:26:56.470
ASUMI

00:26:58.220 --> 00:26:59.220
I'm gonna hit the bathroom.

00:26:59.220 --> 00:27:01.260
I gotta go see how the dog is doing.

00:27:01.260 --> 00:27:02.760
Sorry, got a call from Kiriko.

00:27:02.760 --> 00:27:05.810
Mari, I'd like today's Mari-Special!

00:27:07.940 --> 00:27:11.310
- Huh? Shu, Mrs. Kiriko is right here.
- Oh, Koki! Long time no see!

00:27:11.310 --> 00:27:14.070
- Hello, it's been quite a while. I'll see you later.
- What's going on?

00:27:15.530 --> 00:27:17.030
What's wrong?

00:27:17.030 --> 00:27:18.570
Oh, the Mari-Special!

00:27:37.510 --> 00:27:40.800
The Kizuna Train is running along the tracks
with no brakes.

00:27:41.510 --> 00:27:43.390
There are 150 people inside.

00:27:44.470 --> 00:27:47.850
Up ahead is a woman with her foot stuck
in the tracks and unable to move.

00:27:48.770 --> 00:27:50.060
So here's a question.

00:27:51.230 --> 00:27:56.940
Will you switch the tracks to let the train derail
and sacrifice all of its passengers?

00:27:57.480 --> 00:27:59.860
Or will you let the train keep running...

00:28:02.910 --> 00:28:05.240
and sacrifice the innocent woman?

00:28:06.540 --> 00:28:10.120
Guide the future.

00:28:17.420 --> 00:28:20.300
What was that vision?

00:28:20.930 --> 00:28:23.390
Was it from Asumi?

00:28:25.180 --> 00:28:26.890
What was that just now?

00:28:27.680 --> 00:28:29.520
Why did I get a call from Asumi?

00:28:29.520 --> 00:28:31.640
A phone call assuming the name of the dead...

00:28:31.640 --> 00:28:33.600
Geez, that was in really bad taste.

00:28:33.600 --> 00:28:35.020
Hey, Koki!

00:28:35.440 --> 00:28:36.770
Mr. Shirakaba.

00:28:36.770 --> 00:28:39.490
What are you doing there? A phone call?

00:28:39.490 --> 00:28:40.110
Kaba!

00:28:40.990 --> 00:28:44.700
Shuta, what are you doing in a place like that?

00:28:44.700 --> 00:28:47.950
Well, maybe a change of pace?

00:28:51.250 --> 00:28:53.960
I didn't think the three of you
would be eating a meal together.

00:28:54.540 --> 00:28:56.880
All in all, you guys really do get along.

00:28:56.880 --> 00:28:58.840
<i>What in the world was that scene?</i>

00:28:58.840 --> 00:29:02.260
Sheesh, all three of you are deep in thought.
What's wrong?

00:29:02.260 --> 00:29:05.340
Mrs. Kiriko ate all the Mari-Special
that I made for you guys.

00:29:05.340 --> 00:29:09.810
Geez, you guys are hopeless. All right, let's go!

00:29:10.470 --> 00:29:13.140
- No, I don't feel like it right now.
- Asumi is eagerly waiting for you guys!

00:29:13.140 --> 00:29:15.100
Kaba, you're still as pushy as always.

00:29:15.600 --> 00:29:19.110
All right, all right. I'll go. I will head over.

00:29:19.110 --> 00:29:21.490
Hey, you're being rude to your teacher.

00:29:21.490 --> 00:29:22.610
Yeah, yeah.

00:29:23.280 --> 00:29:24.820
Mr. Shirakaba.

00:29:25.280 --> 00:29:31.080
Thank you so much for thinking about them
like this even after they've graduated.

00:29:31.330 --> 00:29:34.420
This is just my personality,
so please don't worry about it.

00:29:34.750 --> 00:29:39.130
Things like this just don't change
just because I am no longer their teacher.

00:29:40.750 --> 00:29:43.090
This is Sakuragi's family dog.

00:29:45.720 --> 00:29:47.090
<i>Daisy.</i>

00:29:51.390 --> 00:29:52.270
Koki.

00:29:52.430 --> 00:29:53.680
Sakuragi?

00:29:53.680 --> 00:29:55.310
You're still a dog lover, huh?

00:29:55.600 --> 00:29:57.730
They just bring me peace of mind.

00:29:59.610 --> 00:30:00.940
What'll you do, Sakuragi?

00:30:01.360 --> 00:30:04.530
I just saw her two days ago, so...

00:30:05.070 --> 00:30:06.320
I see.

00:30:06.490 --> 00:30:09.240
Please take care of them, sir.

00:30:09.240 --> 00:30:10.740
- I will.
- Take care.

00:30:11.160 --> 00:30:13.370
Don't fight in front of Asumi, okay?

00:30:13.370 --> 00:30:14.710
Like we would.

00:30:15.210 --> 00:30:17.710
Take care!

00:30:20.170 --> 00:30:24.050
Oh, what's wrong, Daisy?
You're acting fussy today.

00:30:24.050 --> 00:30:27.130
We're gonna be heading out as well.

00:30:30.050 --> 00:30:33.100
It's surprisingly crowded today.

00:30:33.810 --> 00:30:36.770
That's right, the opening ceremony
for the Kizuna Train is today!

00:30:37.310 --> 00:30:42.230
But is it all right to open it up like six months
before the originally planned date?

00:30:37.310 --> 00:30:42.900
<i>What was that scene from earlier?
It wasn't just an illusion, was it?</i>

00:30:42.230 --> 00:30:45.530
Who knows? I've heard
rumors that there were various issues.

00:30:43.360 --> 00:30:45.530
Hey, what color was the Kizuna Train?

00:30:45.530 --> 00:30:48.780
Tsuzuragawa was complaining how the construction
company's management was pretty sloppy.

00:30:46.070 --> 00:30:49.370
An ultramarine flying over the seas.

00:30:49.530 --> 00:30:50.660
Ultramarine.

00:30:51.120 --> 00:30:53.330
<i>That train was blue, too.</i>

00:30:53.490 --> 00:30:55.830
<i>Hold on. I need to remember this better.</i>

00:30:56.120 --> 00:30:59.580
<i>What was Mari doing on the tracks
so far away from the station to begin with?</i>

00:31:00.210 --> 00:31:01.540
<i>What was she...</i>

00:31:04.170 --> 00:31:05.050
Daisy?

00:31:06.260 --> 00:31:08.680
Ran, you can hack into a transmitter, right?

00:31:08.680 --> 00:31:10.430
- Depends on the model and operation parameters.
- Wh-What's going on?

00:31:10.680 --> 00:31:14.970
Model. The model number is GP-257S.

00:31:15.180 --> 00:31:19.060
What an enthusiast.
That's the military model from Toki Electrics.

00:31:19.060 --> 00:31:21.810
I think it had a security hole.

00:31:22.230 --> 00:31:25.070
<i>Huh? I'm feeling pretty good today?</i>

00:31:25.360 --> 00:31:27.990
There. I think I can do it. All I need now is—

00:31:27.990 --> 00:31:31.950
- Username is "Tsuduragawa," and the password is...
- You guys aren't doing anything sketchy, right?

00:31:34.200 --> 00:31:35.330
The password is...

00:31:35.370 --> 00:31:37.000
Berliner Pfannkuchen.

00:31:41.040 --> 00:31:42.000
This spot.

00:31:42.500 --> 00:31:44.130
Shuta. Nijimi Station.

00:31:44.130 --> 00:31:44.920
Got it.

00:31:46.670 --> 00:31:48.970
NIJIMI STATION

00:31:47.010 --> 00:31:48.970
Wow, what's that?

00:31:49.590 --> 00:31:52.930
Oh, it's a protest. They're so hyped up.

00:31:52.930 --> 00:31:54.310
Oh, Koki's dad.

00:31:55.390 --> 00:31:57.430
Please ask your questions later!

00:31:57.430 --> 00:31:58.730
Please let us through!

00:31:59.020 --> 00:32:01.850
We've been waiting for you, Mayor Suido.

00:32:01.850 --> 00:32:03.770
We'll be under your care for today.

00:32:03.770 --> 00:32:06.400
The protesters have made their way inside—

00:32:06.400 --> 00:32:07.990
Suido! Abolish Hazard Cast!

00:32:08.820 --> 00:32:09.570
Got him!

00:32:09.570 --> 00:32:10.700
Hold him down!

00:32:11.070 --> 00:32:13.530
Looks like he got too excited and got reckless.

00:32:13.530 --> 00:32:15.620
Violence will only backfire on you.

00:32:15.620 --> 00:32:18.080
Why are there idiots like that?

00:32:18.500 --> 00:32:21.370
I guess we need to call attention to this
within DoRed, too.

00:32:21.370 --> 00:32:23.710
DON'T NEEDLESSLY INCREASE
SECURITY CAMERAS!!

00:32:21.960 --> 00:32:22.710
Yes, hello?

00:32:22.710 --> 00:32:24.420
<i>Hey Mari, where are you right now?</i>

00:32:25.290 --> 00:32:26.380
I'm at Nijimi Station.

00:32:26.380 --> 00:32:27.800
<i>Okay, I need you to listen—</i>

00:32:28.590 --> 00:32:30.130
<i>Hey, what's going on? Hey!</i>

00:32:30.260 --> 00:32:32.800
Daisy, wait! I said wait!

00:32:33.090 --> 00:32:35.180
No, don't go that way!
Sorry, I'll talk to you later!

00:32:35.180 --> 00:32:36.510
Daisy!

00:32:39.140 --> 00:32:41.270
Mari! Mari! Damn it.

00:32:45.150 --> 00:32:49.570
<i>I don't understand it,
but if that scene became reality...</i>

00:32:49.900 --> 00:32:51.490
Ugh, geez!

00:32:51.490 --> 00:32:53.740
Shu! Put this on!

00:32:55.450 --> 00:32:56.870
The ring is part of a pair!

00:32:57.030 --> 00:32:59.040
Shuta! What are you doing!?

00:32:59.040 --> 00:32:59.750
Ko!

00:32:59.750 --> 00:33:01.160
I know.

00:33:01.160 --> 00:33:04.080
Damn it, why does such a disgusting scene...

00:33:04.080 --> 00:33:05.710
I agree with you there.

00:33:07.250 --> 00:33:09.760
<i>What's going on?
My body feels unusually lighter.</i>

00:33:12.720 --> 00:33:16.100
<i>- What's happening? I don't get it at all.
- Would you like to connect with Shuta's Phone?</i>

00:33:16.100 --> 00:33:17.010
Yes!

00:33:17.010 --> 00:33:18.010
<i>Connected.</i>

00:33:18.010 --> 00:33:18.810
<i>Shu!</i>

00:33:18.810 --> 00:33:19.770
Ran?

00:33:19.770 --> 00:33:20.640
<i>We're connected now.</i>

00:33:21.560 --> 00:33:23.770
Shuta, you saw it too, didn't you?

00:33:23.770 --> 00:33:25.190
<i>Then...</i>

00:33:25.400 --> 00:33:27.150
Doesn't look like a coincidence.

00:33:27.360 --> 00:33:29.400
It's just a possibility for now.

00:33:29.400 --> 00:33:34.280
No, one of those two scenes
will become reality, right?

00:33:35.820 --> 00:33:37.370
The mayor has arrived.

00:33:37.490 --> 00:33:40.040
Okay, check the microphone
and ornamental ball.

00:33:45.580 --> 00:33:48.790
This isn't good. Give me a break!

00:33:49.880 --> 00:33:51.550
Did you hear something just now?

00:33:51.550 --> 00:33:54.720
Well, a group of people
are already coming down the stairs.

00:33:55.720 --> 00:33:58.180
<i>I still have time before the train arrives, right?</i>

00:33:58.930 --> 00:34:00.510
I can't make a future like that...

00:34:03.680 --> 00:34:05.940
become reality!

00:34:18.410 --> 00:34:21.040
What's this? My body feels strangely light.

00:34:21.040 --> 00:34:22.240
You too, Ko?

00:34:22.660 --> 00:34:23.700
You too?

00:34:23.700 --> 00:34:25.330
I wonder what's going on?

00:34:25.330 --> 00:34:28.830
Shuta is on a whole different level though.

00:34:31.170 --> 00:34:32.630
I can't catch up to that.

00:34:32.630 --> 00:34:34.670
That's not something a human can do.

00:34:34.880 --> 00:34:37.640
I'll keep heading over to the station.
What about you?

00:34:37.640 --> 00:34:42.470
Little ol' me was heading for this place.
This building.

00:34:43.020 --> 00:34:46.230
I have a light-speed "road" just for me
waiting on the roof.

00:34:46.440 --> 00:34:47.940
I see.

00:34:48.230 --> 00:34:48.940
Tsuzuragawa!

00:34:50.980 --> 00:34:52.650
So you did put one on me.

00:34:53.280 --> 00:34:55.440
Mr. Koki, please use this.

00:34:55.440 --> 00:34:56.280
Thanks.

00:34:57.610 --> 00:34:59.570
So, where was it?

00:34:59.820 --> 00:35:01.030
Behind your collar.

00:35:02.950 --> 00:35:05.080
I told you not to put one on me.

00:35:05.080 --> 00:35:06.660
I am terribly sorry.

00:35:11.460 --> 00:35:14.550
Hey Kinako, can you hear me?

00:35:15.170 --> 00:35:18.510
Huh? Ran, you're earlier than planned.

00:35:18.720 --> 00:35:19.720
<i>You guys ready?</i>

00:35:19.720 --> 00:35:21.930
Yes. I'm sure the Kizuna Train will soon—

00:35:21.930 --> 00:35:23.930
<i>Hey, is there anyone on the tracks?</i>

00:35:23.930 --> 00:35:25.810
Huh? On the tracks?

00:35:27.520 --> 00:35:29.310
Daisy, stop!

00:35:29.730 --> 00:35:33.190
<i>This won't end with a simple scolding!</i>

00:35:34.070 --> 00:35:35.070
Daisy!

00:35:38.490 --> 00:35:39.410
Are you okay?

00:35:44.950 --> 00:35:46.330
H-Huh?

00:35:46.450 --> 00:35:48.460
What should I do? I can't pull my foot out.

00:35:48.620 --> 00:35:51.460
What a disaster!
There really is someone on the tracks!

00:35:51.460 --> 00:35:53.130
Wait, that's Mari?

00:35:53.250 --> 00:35:55.250
Whoa!

00:35:57.090 --> 00:35:59.720
<i>What should we do? We have to go save her!</i>

00:35:59.720 --> 00:36:02.890
You won't make it from there.
I have an idea...

00:36:03.680 --> 00:36:06.430
Huh? What? A standalone?

00:36:06.770 --> 00:36:09.980
The Kizuna Train's sales pitch was that
it's fully autonomous and auto-piloted, right?

00:36:09.980 --> 00:36:13.860
I don't believe this!
It's like they want to cause an accident.

00:36:11.190 --> 00:36:15.020
An immense amount of data
is required for Hazard Cast,

00:36:14.270 --> 00:36:16.900
<i>So the rumor was true about
Kizuna's construction and maintenance</i>

00:36:15.020 --> 00:36:17.610
and people fear the infiltration of criminals
from outside of this ward.

00:36:16.900 --> 00:36:20.070
<i>being shoddy
because they rushed completion.</i>

00:36:18.150 --> 00:36:21.110
However, Kizuna is fully autonomous,

00:36:21.410 --> 00:36:24.030
and is equipped with the latest scanners.

00:36:22.990 --> 00:36:24.740
We'll be doing the same thing in the end.

00:36:24.030 --> 00:36:26.490
It'll sense all the potential criminals beforehand.

00:36:25.410 --> 00:36:26.870
Kinako, what about the drone?

00:36:26.870 --> 00:36:29.710
<i>It's already set up within the station.
We can use it any time!</i>

00:36:26.870 --> 00:36:32.630
By preventing their entry before it happens,
we can protect the safety and security of the ward.

00:36:29.710 --> 00:36:31.330
Kinako, I'm borrowing your PC.

00:36:31.330 --> 00:36:32.960
Confirming hub connection.

00:36:35.420 --> 00:36:38.800
<i>I have to operate the drone while rewriting
the program I had already prepared.</i>

00:36:39.010 --> 00:36:40.720
<i>The endorphins are through the roof!</i>

00:36:43.590 --> 00:36:44.300
Sheesh!

00:36:50.020 --> 00:36:52.900
Helping out the weak is what my art's about!

00:36:53.190 --> 00:36:54.400
Take off!

00:36:58.030 --> 00:36:58.980
What's that?

00:36:59.150 --> 00:37:00.990
- Hey, what's that drone?
- Is that a terrorist?

00:37:00.990 --> 00:37:02.360
That's a drone from DoRed!

00:37:02.660 --> 00:37:03.360
This drone is...

00:37:03.360 --> 00:37:06.330
<i>Autocratic Ward Mayor Gori Suido.</i>

00:37:06.330 --> 00:37:10.370
<i>The track that Kizuna is running on,
1,000 meters before the junction to the depot.</i>

00:37:10.620 --> 00:37:13.120
Deploy a rescue team there now.

00:37:13.420 --> 00:37:16.170
<i>There's a girl and a dog
that can't move from that spot.</i>

00:37:15.130 --> 00:37:16.840
This guy is such a stinker.

00:37:16.500 --> 00:37:20.420
<i>At this rate, they'll be run over
by the Kizuna Train and die.</i>

00:37:21.970 --> 00:37:23.470
- I'll shoot it down.
- Don't make a fuss.

00:37:23.470 --> 00:37:25.550
Hana, calm down.

00:37:27.760 --> 00:37:31.140
Do you think the accident
from that scene will really happen?

00:37:31.520 --> 00:37:36.020
There's no way I'd know.
But considering the circumstantial evidence...

00:37:36.110 --> 00:37:38.150
Why is my body so light?

00:37:38.150 --> 00:37:39.780
<i>Does it have something to do
with that call from Asumi?</i>

00:37:39.780 --> 00:37:43.650
There's no way we'd receive a call
from the dead. However...

00:37:43.650 --> 00:37:44.700
That scene...

00:37:44.700 --> 00:37:47.450
It felt like my brain had been hacked directly.

00:37:47.450 --> 00:37:51.250
Even little ol' me don't know tech like that.

00:37:51.540 --> 00:37:54.000
Hackers aren't magicians, after all!

00:37:54.120 --> 00:37:56.750
It would be easier to understand
if this was all magic!

00:37:56.750 --> 00:38:00.420
I mean, I'm leaping over buildings right now!

00:38:00.670 --> 00:38:04.130
We have urban legends and the occult
happening one after another.

00:38:06.430 --> 00:38:09.220
But it's also true
that we have to go along with it.

00:38:09.220 --> 00:38:11.270
Yeah! I don't want it to happen!

00:38:11.310 --> 00:38:13.890
Both of them had the worst results possible!

00:38:14.440 --> 00:38:19.980
<i>I'm sure Asumi is telling us to save them.</i>

00:38:23.570 --> 00:38:27.870
Please don't lean over!
It's dangerous, so please don't lean over!

00:38:27.870 --> 00:38:28.820
- Oh, no.
- Huh?

00:38:28.820 --> 00:38:30.120
U-Um...

00:38:30.120 --> 00:38:31.490
What is it?

00:38:31.490 --> 00:38:35.330
This is about one kilometer ahead of the drone.

00:38:35.620 --> 00:38:38.790
There really is a woman and a dog there.

00:38:36.370 --> 00:38:40.210
Huh? What? My cPhone is missing.
Oh, no, what should I do?

00:38:39.130 --> 00:38:40.210
What?

00:38:40.630 --> 00:38:43.420
Chief! There really is
a woman and a dog out there!

00:38:43.420 --> 00:38:44.130
What?

00:38:44.130 --> 00:38:46.130
The Kizuna Train will be here soon.

00:38:44.590 --> 00:38:45.420
Chief.

00:38:45.420 --> 00:38:47.180
Yes, we'll send a rescue unit right away.

00:38:47.180 --> 00:38:49.890
No, contact the control room first.

00:38:49.890 --> 00:38:53.350
We need to remotely operate the Kizuna Train
and have it come to an emergency stop.

00:38:53.640 --> 00:38:55.100
Y-Yes, sir.

00:38:56.980 --> 00:38:58.770
Hey! You can't just barge in here!

00:38:58.770 --> 00:38:59.730
I'm with the SARG!

00:38:59.730 --> 00:39:02.190
It's not accepting the emergency stop signal?

00:39:00.110 --> 00:39:02.190
This is an emergency! I'm coming through!

00:39:02.440 --> 00:39:04.360
Wh-Why did it end up like that?

00:39:04.360 --> 00:39:07.450
<i>You're the ones who made us work fast
so we'd make it on time!</i>

00:39:07.740 --> 00:39:10.950
We didn't have enough time to test anything,
so these things are bound to happen!

00:39:11.370 --> 00:39:15.000
<i>We're trying to do something about it,
but we don't have enough time!</i>

00:39:15.000 --> 00:39:16.460
I-I can't accept—

00:39:16.460 --> 00:39:20.540
<i>It's impossible! The Kizuna Train
will not stop until it arrives at the station!</i>

00:39:22.130 --> 00:39:25.260
I'm terribly sorry.
This is a miscommunication on my end!

00:39:25.260 --> 00:39:29.430
For now, it's the Kizuna Train.
We must rescue that woman somehow.

00:39:29.930 --> 00:39:30.970
I'll head over.

00:39:30.970 --> 00:39:31.970
Counting on you.

00:39:31.970 --> 00:39:33.010
Will you make it?

00:39:33.010 --> 00:39:36.980
It's less than two minutes
before the Kizuna arrives. It seems a bit tight.

00:39:37.440 --> 00:39:41.480
We don't know what will happen,
so someone needs to be close-by regardless.

00:39:39.230 --> 00:39:40.480
SARG! Everyone stay put!

00:39:42.230 --> 00:39:45.230
Can you switch rails at the junction
the drone was talking about?

00:39:45.230 --> 00:39:49.320
It's possible.
But at that speed, it will very likely derail.

00:39:49.320 --> 00:39:53.120
But at this rate, that woman
will definitely get run over, right?

00:39:53.120 --> 00:39:55.750
Yes, that's true, but...

00:39:54.410 --> 00:39:57.160
<i>This is just like the trolley dilemma.</i>

00:39:57.370 --> 00:40:02.170
If I didn't save a woman
who would otherwise have been run over,

00:40:02.170 --> 00:40:03.460
the public would never forgive me.

00:40:03.460 --> 00:40:04.590
You can't!

00:40:06.130 --> 00:40:06.920
Koki.

00:40:06.920 --> 00:40:11.090
If you switch the tracks, the train will derail
and even more people will die!

00:40:11.390 --> 00:40:13.350
You show up suddenly and tell me that?

00:40:13.350 --> 00:40:14.640
Children should stay quiet.

00:40:14.810 --> 00:40:17.390
No, I will not.

00:40:21.440 --> 00:40:23.360
<i>As I suspected, he can't decide.</i>

00:40:23.360 --> 00:40:26.320
<i>In order to save both,
I have to mobilize my own father.</i>

00:40:26.320 --> 00:40:29.700
This is an important period
before our transition to Tokyo.

00:40:27.150 --> 00:40:30.820
<i>For some reason, I have a feeling
about what I should say to him.</i>

00:40:29.700 --> 00:40:31.740
I can't afford to make the wrong decision.

00:40:31.320 --> 00:40:35.280
<i>But at the worst,
this decision will leave Sakuragi to die.</i>

00:40:32.070 --> 00:40:37.410
Chief, tell the control room to switch the rails.
I will take responsibility for it.

00:40:35.700 --> 00:40:37.870
<i>What will you do, Koki Suido?</i>

00:40:37.410 --> 00:40:39.210
U-Understood.

00:40:39.500 --> 00:40:41.790
Mayor... No, Father.

00:40:39.910 --> 00:40:41.420
And get a rescue squad.

00:40:42.210 --> 00:40:43.580
Mother and Asumi...

00:40:48.960 --> 00:40:51.010
Chief, hold on.

00:40:51.340 --> 00:40:52.260
Yes, sir.

00:40:55.050 --> 00:40:57.140
Don't switch the rails.

00:40:57.140 --> 00:40:59.140
Stop the train at any cost!

00:40:59.140 --> 00:41:00.350
Y-Yes, sir!

00:41:00.690 --> 00:41:04.020
Calling all hands,
we will not switch the rails of the Kizuna!

00:41:04.020 --> 00:41:05.690
We will not switch the rails!

00:41:05.690 --> 00:41:08.230
Now Ran, you're up next.

00:41:11.070 --> 00:41:12.780
I'm fully aware of that!

00:41:12.910 --> 00:41:16.780
If the phone doesn't work,
you have to knock on the door directly.

00:41:17.080 --> 00:41:22.750
Even if it's standalone, Kizuna operates
under Japan's 600-meter clause.

00:41:23.000 --> 00:41:28.550
In other words, if we can get the emergency brakes
to deploy, it should stop within 600 meters.

00:41:28.800 --> 00:41:33.970
I'll deploy that emergency brake
as far away from Maririn as possible!

00:41:39.640 --> 00:41:40.640
Brakes!

00:41:42.270 --> 00:41:45.150
Oh, no. The train isn't stopping.

00:41:45.480 --> 00:41:48.270
No! At this rate, you'll die too!

00:41:48.650 --> 00:41:49.820
No, you can't!

00:41:51.780 --> 00:41:54.280
You dummy. I don't care anymore!

00:41:54.990 --> 00:41:58.370
Now, this is everything little ol' me can do.

00:41:58.870 --> 00:42:02.620
You're the only one who can save Sakuragi.

00:42:03.160 --> 00:42:04.540
Go, Shuta.

00:42:05.580 --> 00:42:09.590
Leave it to me!

00:42:55.010 --> 00:42:56.260
Shu!

00:42:56.840 --> 00:42:59.010
Asumi shielded me, and....

00:42:59.550 --> 00:43:02.010
You can save her, right?

00:43:02.260 --> 00:43:04.520
You're a hero, right?

00:43:04.980 --> 00:43:07.270
- Stop. Stop it.
- Please!

00:43:07.560 --> 00:43:09.360
Why am I thinking about this again?

00:43:10.440 --> 00:43:13.440
Back then, I couldn't make it in time.

00:43:14.490 --> 00:43:20.240
I can still feel Asumi's body
getting cold in my arms.

00:43:20.830 --> 00:43:23.200
I beg you, go away.

00:43:23.700 --> 00:43:27.250
Shuta, don't stop being a hero.

00:43:27.750 --> 00:43:29.460
But I...

00:43:31.380 --> 00:43:33.300
No. Just for now...

00:43:34.420 --> 00:43:36.470
I am a hero!

00:43:37.220 --> 00:43:39.970
That's right!
This is a chance that Asumi is giving me!

00:43:40.930 --> 00:43:44.560
The future? I'll change it into my ideal future!

00:43:48.730 --> 00:43:49.520
I will...

00:43:50.440 --> 00:43:51.480
I will...

00:43:53.690 --> 00:43:55.610
save everything!

00:43:56.110 --> 00:43:58.030
Mari!

00:43:58.030 --> 00:43:58.860
Shu?

00:44:01.660 --> 00:44:05.410
Reach!

00:44:25.350 --> 00:44:26.890
I made it!

00:44:26.890 --> 00:44:28.270
Sh-Shu?

00:44:28.430 --> 00:44:30.520
- There she is!
- Where's the ambulance?

00:44:28.770 --> 00:44:30.980
Huh? How? Why are you here?

00:44:32.610 --> 00:44:35.780
I wonder, too.
I really don't know all too well myself.

00:44:35.780 --> 00:44:39.320
- Huh? Hey, I really don't get what's going on.
- Crap.

00:44:39.820 --> 00:44:41.610
Mari, don't tell anyone!

00:44:41.610 --> 00:44:43.240
Huh? What do you mean?

00:44:51.580 --> 00:44:55.540
Ran, is this some kind of
performance or something?

00:44:55.880 --> 00:45:00.170
<i>Well, a slightly strange incident happened, huh?</i>

00:45:00.170 --> 00:45:01.430
<i>Strange?</i>

00:45:03.260 --> 00:45:06.510
I was planning on
graffiti-bombing that train, too.

00:45:06.510 --> 00:45:08.720
<i>But you were really awesome!</i>

00:45:08.850 --> 00:45:10.600
Thank you, Kinako.

00:45:10.940 --> 00:45:14.440
Mayor Suido! Can we get a comment from you
regarding this incident?

00:45:14.440 --> 00:45:16.110
Was it because the opening ceremony
was conducted ahead of schedule?

00:45:14.810 --> 00:45:16.900
This is believed to be a question of liability,
but do you have any explanation?

00:45:16.110 --> 00:45:17.570
You couldn't have predicted this
using Hazard Cast?

00:45:17.570 --> 00:45:19.360
Silence please, everyone!

00:45:19.860 --> 00:45:22.950
A huge accident
has been prevented before it happened.

00:45:23.410 --> 00:45:26.870
However, we don't know when danger
will strike again.

00:45:24.740 --> 00:45:27.740
<i>My choice in that one moment...</i>

00:45:27.330 --> 00:45:30.120
For perfect security
with Special Administrative Region Guard,

00:45:28.870 --> 00:45:30.120
Tsuzuragawa.

00:45:30.120 --> 00:45:32.620
we need a complete redevelopment...

00:45:30.750 --> 00:45:33.920
Find out who called me on this.

00:45:34.080 --> 00:45:34.880
Sure.

00:45:36.590 --> 00:45:37.500
This is...

00:45:39.090 --> 00:45:42.130
I'll hold off with this for today.

00:45:48.140 --> 00:45:50.060
Those guys...

00:45:50.890 --> 00:45:53.770
Go pay your proper respects to Asumi, okay?

00:45:57.730 --> 00:46:00.230
Hey, when are we gonna tell Kaba?

00:46:00.230 --> 00:46:01.320
Tell him what?

00:46:01.320 --> 00:46:05.200
Huh? I mean, the fact that Asumi
might still be alive.

00:46:05.740 --> 00:46:06.910
Shu.

00:46:06.910 --> 00:46:09.910
You heard the voice over the phone, right?
It was Asumi's voice.

00:46:10.410 --> 00:46:11.660
She's alive, right?

00:46:11.660 --> 00:46:13.540
- That's why we heard her voice, right?
- Shu, that's not it.

00:46:13.540 --> 00:46:16.080
Did you guys actually know about this?

00:46:16.080 --> 00:46:17.590
- Shu, that's enough.
- You're her big brother, Koki.

00:46:17.590 --> 00:46:18.790
Stop it already!

00:46:19.460 --> 00:46:22.800
My sister is dead! Asumi Suido is dead!

00:46:22.970 --> 00:46:25.800
That can't be true!
You heard that voice, too!

00:46:25.890 --> 00:46:27.930
You can fabricate things like that!

00:46:27.930 --> 00:46:29.310
Asumi is dead!

00:46:31.470 --> 00:46:32.600
Punch me.

00:46:33.060 --> 00:46:34.850
Punch me if that's what you wanna do!

00:46:41.780 --> 00:46:44.030
You have to properly face reality.

00:46:44.360 --> 00:46:45.990
Are you gonna run away?

00:46:45.990 --> 00:46:47.950
- That's what you're doing.
- Hey, Koki!

00:46:48.320 --> 00:46:48.910
Koki!

00:46:48.910 --> 00:46:49.870
Shu!

00:46:50.410 --> 00:46:52.160
Asumin is dead.

00:46:52.540 --> 00:46:57.170
That was someone else
pretending to be Asumin.

00:47:08.720 --> 00:47:10.010
Shuta.

00:47:11.970 --> 00:47:15.520
You're amazing.
You really did come to save me.

00:47:18.020 --> 00:47:21.770
You really are a hero after all, Shuta.

00:47:21.770 --> 00:47:22.820
Asumi.

00:47:24.150 --> 00:47:27.320
<i>That's not it... I...</i>

00:47:28.910 --> 00:47:31.780
<i>No. Asumi is still alive.</i>

00:47:33.240 --> 00:47:34.870
<i>You're still alive, aren't you?</i>

00:47:45.590 --> 00:47:48.050
Select your future.

00:47:49.970 --> 00:47:52.260
<i>Establish a future...</i>

00:47:55.100 --> 00:47:57.060
<i>...in my place.</i>
